---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="About Us — Snake Game Online"
  description="Snake Game is the classic arcade game, sharpened for your browser. Free, no account, no ads, and playable on any device. Learn about the game and who built it."
  eyebrow="ABOUT SNAKE GAME"
  heading="The classic, sharpened for your browser."
  kicker="Snake Game is a free online recreation of the arcade classic — rebuilt for modern browsers with no downloads, no accounts, and no ads."
>
  <p>
    Snake Game is the classic arcade game of growing a snake on a square board. You steer the
    snake toward the fruit; every fruit you eat adds a segment and scores points. The board
    never grows, so the longer you get, the harder every turn becomes — hit a wall or your own
    tail and the run is over.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we built it</h2>
  <p>
    The game runs entirely in your browser. There is nothing to install, no account to create,
    and no advertisement to sit through — you press <strong>Space</strong> and you are playing.
    Everything, including your best scores and the daily challenge, is stored on your own
    device, so you are never locked in to a server or a login.
  </p>

  <h2>Four ways to play</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Classic</strong> — the original rules. Eat fruit, grow, and don't hit the wall
      or your own tail.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Time Attack</strong> — 60 seconds on the clock. Same rules as Classic, but the
      clock is your opponent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Zen</strong> — walls wrap around. Leave one edge and you appear on the other;
      only your own tail can end the run.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Daily</strong> — a seeded challenge for your local calendar day. Complete the
      day's 60 fruits to keep your streak alive.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Privacy by design</h2>
  <p>
    We do not collect personal data, and we never will. The game is fully client-side, your
    scores live only in your browser's local storage, and the only analytics we use are
    anonymous page-view and gameplay events. See the
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}privacy/`}>Privacy Policy</a> for the full picture.
  </p>

  <h2>Who built it</h2>
  <p>
    Snake Game is built and maintained by Yash Kharb. It is free to play — if you have
    feedback, a feature request, or just found a bug, <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}contact/`}>get in touch</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>